:[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":3},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["roots_bound",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":5,"beg":{"line":204,"col":4},"end":{"line":227,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":"pub(crate) fn roots_bound(budget: usize) -> Result<WorkUnits, DecodeError> {\n        let r = number(budget)?;\n        let leaves = mul(160, r)?;\n        if budget < 3 {\n            return Ok(WorkUnits(leaves));\n        }\n        // Expanding one node's exact table gives 12812*d^2 + 17486*d + 16968.\n        // Closed sums keep request admission O(B), independent of algebraic degree.\n        let next = add(r, 1)?;\n        let squares = mul(mul(r, next)?, add(mul(2, r)?, 1)?)? / 6;\n        let linear = mul(r, next)? / 2;\n        let squares = squares\n            .checked_sub(5)\n            .ok_or(DecodeError::WorkLimitExceeded)?;\n        let linear = linear\n            .checked_sub(3)\n            .ok_or(DecodeError::WorkLimitExceeded)?;\n        let nodes = r.checked_sub(2).ok_or(DecodeError::WorkLimitExceeded)?;\n        let total = add(\n            add(mul(12812, squares)?, mul(17486, linear)?)?,\n            mul(16968, nodes)?,\n        )?;\n        Ok(WorkUnits(add(leaves, total)?))\n    }","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Worst proper split tree. For increasing convex node costs, an unbalanced"},{"DocComment":" chain maximizes their sum: at most one node of each size 3..=r is sufficient"},{"DocComment":" as a bound. At each node all 64 trace directions and split checks are charged."},{"DocComment":" 160*r additionally bounds every possible degree-one/two leaf partition."},{"Builtin":{"Inline":["Always",{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":5,"beg":{"line":203,"col":4},"end":{"line":203,"col":21}},"generated_from_span":null}}]}}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":false},"is_local":true,"started_from":true,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item